{# A range input always posts a value, even when nothing was ever stored — with
   an empty `value` the browser parks the thumb at the midpoint of min/max, and
   the first save of the page writes THAT. So a field whose PHP side has a
   sensible fallback has to declare the same number as `'default'` here, or the
   fallback is silently replaced by ~50 the moment someone saves the tab.

   The default must also be REACHABLE by the slider — on-step and inside
   min/max. See the note on the mirror input below for what happens otherwise.

   The test is against '' only: get_option() gives false for an unset option
   (false == '' in PHP), while a deliberate 0 or '0' is a real value and is kept. #}
{% set field_value = (value == '') ? (val.default ?? '') : value %}
<label for="{{ name }}">
    <input type="range"
        class="custom-options-{{ val.type }}"
        name="{{ name }}"
        id="{{ name }}"
        value="{{ field_value|esc_attr }}"
        min="{{ val.tweaks.min }}"
        max="{{ val.tweaks.max }}"
        step="{{ val.tweaks.step }}"
    />
    {# The number box is a DISPLAY MIRROR of the slider: it carries no `name`,
       posts nothing, and the range beside it is the value that actually saves.
       It still takes part in HTML5 constraint validation though, and that once
       broke the whole page: with min="2" step="2" only even numbers validate, so
       a stored odd value made the box fail stepMismatch and the browser refused
       to submit the FORM — silently, because the box sits on an inactive tab
       where it is display:none and cannot be focused to show the message
       ("An invalid form control with name='' is not focusable"). Every setting
       on the page stopped saving because of a control that saves nothing.

       step="any" keeps the box out of that: the range still enforces the real
       stepping, and re-syncs the box from itself on blur. min/max stay for the
       spinner bounds — they can only bite while the field is visible, where the
       browser can actually show the user what is wrong. #}
    <input
        type="number"
        class="val_{{ name }}_display"
        value="{{ field_value|esc_attr }}"
        min="{{ val.tweaks.min }}"
        max="{{ val.tweaks.max }}"
        step="any"
    > <span class="suffix">{{ val.tweaks.suffix }}</span>
    {% if description %}
    <p class="description">{{ description }}</p>
    {% endif %}
</label>
